        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "I would not extend this box. I would mark it reviewed and leave it on today’s outbound manifest for the 14:30 destruction collection.\n\nThere is no written duty-manager permission registered for a date change. The 9 October note is only a pending request for tomorrow’s sitting, and a pending request is not permission. Operators do not grant discretionary extensions; this morning’s instruction was no discretionary extensions this cycle and to release the full batch on time. A collection booking, a contact note, or an internal message does not change a storage date or take a box off the manifest. Permission registered later would not cover a change made today. Holding the whole manifest past 13:30 would stop every dispatch and record the shift as incomplete, which the policy does not allow.",
